course: dictionary
lesson: 4092
title: Big words about size
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how big something is. Gigantism comes from giant, and it names the state of becoming very large. Read the clues around it: «On islands with no predators, some small animals become giants, like the giant rats of Flores and giant tortoises; this is called island gigantism.»
explain: The sentence starts with small animals and ends with giants, so the clue is that gigantism means becoming much bigger than usual. The words «this is called» show that the new word names that change. Put your meaning in place of the hard word: "animals become very big" fits, so you are on the right track.
explain: Gigantism has a second meaning, in medicine. It is a rare condition in which a child grows far taller than usual. Here the word describes a health problem, not an animal, so the subject of the sentence tells you which meaning is meant.
fact: Gigantism is a noun, so it names a thing or a state.
fact: Gigantism means being very large in size.
fact: «Island gigantism» means small animals on islands becoming much bigger than their relatives.
fact: Giant tortoises and the giant rats of Flores are examples of island gigantism.
fact: In medicine, gigantism is a rare condition where a child grows far taller than usual.
exercise: «On islands with no predators, some small animals become giants.» What does island gigantism describe? | Plants that grow in the sea | Animals that fly away from islands | *Small animals becoming much bigger than their relatives | Animals losing their colour
exercise: Nadia says gigantism is just a fancy word for small. What does it really mean? | Running very fast | Being very small and quiet | Living under the sea | *Being very large in size
exercise: Which word in «giant tortoises» has the same root as gigantism? | Predators | *Giant | Tortoises | Islands
test: A doctor says a boy has gigantism because he grows far taller than other children his age. What is gigantism in this sentence? | A type of stormy weather | A kind of sweet food | *A rare condition in which a child grows far taller than usual | A game played on islands
test: Scientists studied island gigantism in giant tortoises, which were far bigger than their mainland relatives. What does the word far tell you? | That the tortoises lived far away from the sea | That the tortoises were hard to find | That the tortoises moved slowly | *That the tortoises were much bigger, not just a little
exam: Jayden says gigantism means small. Using the sentence «some small animals become giants», why is he wrong? | Because islands are always small | Because gigantism is a verb that means to shrink | *Because the sentence says small animals become giants, so gigantism means becoming much bigger | Because giants are never real animals
